IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-additional`

-- ccc18-tests-soira-additional.l4 -- tests for ccc18-soira-additional.l4. Expected values are written from the text of the Criminal Code
-- (R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, lines 10275-10956 of the plain-text rendering), beside each assertion, and not copied from the module's own output.

#ASSERT `s 490.04(1) the person may apply to a court for an exemption order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 490.04(1) the person may apply to a court for an exemption order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 490.04(1) the person may apply to a court for an exemption order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.04(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.04(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.04(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(b)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an application under paragraph (1)(a)

#ASSERT `s 490.04(3) the court to which the application shall be made` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 490.04(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 490.04(3) the court to which the application shall be made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 490.04(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 490.04(3) the court to which the application shall be made` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 490.04(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 490.04(3) the court to which the application shall be made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 490.04(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`

#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): indictment, two years or more, victim under 18
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a) needs all three: the victim was not under 18
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a): a sentence under two years
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a): not prosecuted by indictment
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.04(4) the court shall not make an exemption order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the limitation is for an application under paragraph (1)(a)

#ASSERT `s 490.04(5) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.04(5) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 2 of 2 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.04(5) the court shall make an exemption order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
#ASSERT `s 490.04(5) the court shall make an exemption order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.04(5) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.04(5) make an exemption order` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.04 the court shall make an exemption order, subject to subsection (4)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the limitation overrides
#ASSERT `s 490.04 the court shall make an exemption order, subject to subsection (4)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.04 the court shall make an exemption order, subject to subsection (4)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 490.04 the court shall make an exemption order, subject to subsection (4)` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 490.04(6): each factor in the list is one the court shall consider, when it is determining the order; (g) adds any matter the court considers relevant.

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the order or obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the court considers it relevant: paragraph (g)

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` TRUE `s 490.04(6) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not named, and the court does not consider it relevant

#ASSERT `s 490.04(6) the court shall consider the factor` FALSE `s 490.04(6)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the order or obligation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not determining the order

#ASSERT `s 490.04(7) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.04(7) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.04(7) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.04(7) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.04(8) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.04(8) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.04(8) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.04(8) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) needs no offence with a life maximum
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (c) needs the obligation to have begun before the day
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (c) needs the condition of paragraph 490.029051(1)(b)
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.05(1) the person may apply to a court for a variation order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.05(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.05(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.05(2) the person is not permitted to apply under paragraph (1)(c) or (d)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.05(3) the court to which the application shall be made` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 490.05(3)(a) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 490.05(3) the court to which the application shall be made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 490.05(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 490.05(3) the court to which the application shall be made` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 490.05(3)(b) a court of criminal jurisdiction`

#ASSERT `s 490.05(4) the court shall make the variation order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- ground 1 of 1 alone
#ASSERT `s 490.05(4) the court shall make the variation order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court is not satisfied of any ground
-- the text gives no time for the order, so the trace has no WITHIN; the court makes the order: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.05(4) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.05(4) make the variation order` AT 1

-- 490.05(5): (b) and (c) apply paragraphs (a) and (b) of 490.022(3) / 490.02904(3): two or five years -> 10 years after; 10 or 14 -> 20 years after; sentenced 1 June 2012.
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(c) an obligation under section 490.02901` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(c) an obligation under section 490.02901` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2032))
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019` TRUE `imprisonment for life` (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- only paragraphs (a) and (b) are applied
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(a) an order under section 490.012` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) (JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (Date 1 6 2022))   -- 490.013(2)'s answer, taken as an input
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(a) an order under section 490.012` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(d) an obligation under section 36.1 of the International Transfer of Offenders Act` TRUE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING (JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`) EQUALS JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- the other Act's answer, taken as an input
#ASSERT `s 490.05(5) the duration set out in the variation order` `s 490.05(5)(b) an obligation under section 490.019` FALSE (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`) (Date 1 6 2012) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- no variation order made
#TRACE `s 490.05(5) the duty of the court to set out the duration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.05(5) set out the duration of the order or obligation in the variation order` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.05(6) the court shall give reasons for its decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.05(6) the court shall give reasons for its decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.05(6) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.05(6) give reasons for its decision` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.05(7) the court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.05(7) the court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.05(7) the duty of the court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 490.05(7) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.06(1) the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.06(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.06(1) another person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.06(1) the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a different decision
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal may be brought` `s 490.06(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a ground raising no question of law or mixed law and fact

#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) dismiss the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.04(5) or section 490.05` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(1) the appeal court may do it` `s 490.06(1) another thing` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 490.06(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.06(2) the appeal court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.06(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.06(2) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of a copy of the order made under section 490.012, the notice referred to in section 490.02901 or the Form 1 referred to in subparagraph 8(4)(a)(ii) of the International Transfer of Offenders Act, as the case may be` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.07(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.07(1) the appeal court shall cause the notification and the information to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 490.07(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the Commissioner and the Attorney General to be notified` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.07(1) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1
#TRACE `s 490.07(1) the duty of the appeal court to cause the person to be informed of the sections` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.07(1) cause the person who applied for the order to be informed of sections 4 to 7.1 of the Sex Offender Information Registration Act, sections 490.031 and 490.0311 of this Act and section 119.1 of the National Defence Act` AT 1

#ASSERT `s 490.07(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 490.07(2) the appeal court shall cause the notification to be given` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text gives no time for the act, so the trace has no WITHIN; the party does the act: expected FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 490.07(2) the duty of a court of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a court of appeal` DOES `s 490.07(2) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of the decision` AT 1
